# The ledger of `config`: what Go's viper (1.20.1), godotenv (1.5.1) and
# envconfig (1.4.0), Rust's config (0.15), dotenvy (0.15) and figment (0.10),
# and Python's python-dotenv (1.2.4), pydantic-settings (2.16.3) and dynaconf
# (3.2.13) let a program do with its settings, one block per capability, and
# what Rebel answers. None of the nine is a standard library, so the lists are
# their documentation on this machine, 2026-11-17: `go doc -all` of viper and
# godotenv from the module cache and of envconfig fetched into the scratch
# folder; the names of `cargo doc`'s `all.html` and of each type's page for
# the three crates, built in the scratch folder; `dir()` of `dotenv`,
# `dotenv.main`, `pydantic_settings`, `dynaconf` and `dynaconf.base.Settings`,
# `SettingsConfigDict`'s keys and `inspect.signature` of python-dotenv's
# functions. Every expected value of the package's tests that one of them
# answers was observed from godotenv, dotenvy and python-dotenv, viper and
# pydantic, the same day.

capability config/layers  settings read from several sources and merged, each source over the ones before it
  heroes  config.Layer, config.merge
  go      viper.New, NewWithOptions, GetViper, Viper, Reset, MergeConfig, MergeConfigMap, MergeInConfig
  rust    config::Config::builder, ConfigBuilder::add_source, ConfigBuilder::build, ConfigBuilder::build_cloned, figment::Figment::new, Figment::from, Figment::merge, Figment::join
  python  pydantic_settings.BaseSettings.settings_customise_sources, InitSettingsSource, dynaconf.Dynaconf, dynaconf.LazySettings, Settings.update, Settings.execute_loaders, Settings.pre_load
  note    a program lists its layers, the lowest first, and says the precedence by that order: viper's fixed order (override, flag, env, file, key-value store, default) and figment's `join` (the earlier wins) are both an order of the list

capability config/deep-merge  an object over an object merged member by member, any other value replacing what stood
  heroes  config.merge
  go      MergeConfig, MergeConfigMap
  rust    figment::Figment::merge
  python  dynaconf merge_enabled, dynaconf_merge
  note    an object over an object is merged key by key as viper, figment's `merge` and config-rs merge them, and any other value replaces what stood, keeping its place. A `null` sets nothing, as viper's `null` over a default or over a table: viper's merge of two files lets a `null` leaf erase the value below (observed 2026-11-17, `host: null` over `host: localhost` reads nil) while a `null` over a default does not; one rule here, so that a key with nothing under it in YAML never erases a setting

capability config/list-append  a list of one source joined to the same list of the source below it
  heroes  refused: a list is one setting, so that a message names the one layer that wrote it; a program that wants two lists joined reads each layer's list with `layer_at` and `json.items_of` and sets the joined one with `set_value`
  go      -
  rust    figment::Figment::adjoin, Figment::admerge
  python  dynaconf dynaconf_merge on a list, `@merge`
  note    -

