capability config/override  values a program sets over every source
  heroes  config.set_value, config.merge
  go      Set
  rust    config::ConfigBuilder::set_override, set_override_option
  python  InitSettingsSource, dynaconf Settings.set, Settings.unset, Settings.unset_all
  note    an override is the last layer a program lists; `set_value` writes it

capability config/formats  a settings text in TOML, YAML, JSON or INI read into a layer
  heroes  config.Format, config.parse_layer
  go      SetConfigType, ReadConfig, SupportedExts, Codec, Decoder, CodecRegistry, DefaultCodecRegistry, NewCodecRegistry, WithCodecRegistry, DecoderRegistry, WithDecoderRegistry
  rust    config::File::from_str, FileFormat, FileFormat::parse, FileSourceString, Format, FileStoredFormat, figment::providers::Toml, Json, Yaml, YamlExtended, Data::string, Format::string
  python  TomlConfigSettingsSource, YamlConfigSettingsSource, JsonConfigSettingsSource, PyprojectTomlConfigSettingsSource, dynaconf loaders
  note    TOML's dates become their RFC 3339 text through `toml.to_json`, read back with `instant_of`; INI's sections are objects of texts, keys before the first section at the top, `DEFAULT`'s keys filled into each section as Python's configparser reads them, viper 1.20.1 having no INI decoder compiled in (observed: `decoder not found for this format`). A program that reads TOML carries `time`, which `toml` uses: 1.66 MB more in a program of `json`, `yaml`, `ini`, `flags` and `os` (2,261,088 against 3,923,776 bytes, built 2026-11-17)

capability config/formats-other  JSON5, RON, HCL and Java properties
