capability config/profiles  the settings of one profile (development, production) chosen among a file's tables, over its defaults
  heroes  config.layer_at, config.merge
  go      -
  rust    figment::Profile, Profile::const_new, Figment::select, Figment::profile, Figment::profiles, Data::profile, Serialized::global, Env::global, Env::profile
  python  dynaconf environments, Settings.from_env, using_env, current_env, setenv, loaded_envs, namespace, current_namespace, using_namespace, loaded_namespaces
  note    a profile is a table of a file: `merge([layer_at(file, "default"), layer_at(file, "production")])` is figment's `select` and dynaconf's environments; which profile is the program's to read, from a variable or a flag

capability config/env  the environment's variables of one prefix read into a layer
  heroes  config.from_env, config.read_env, config.EnvOptions, config.env_options
  go      SetEnvPrefix, GetEnvPrefix, AutomaticEnv
  rust    config::Environment::with_prefix, Environment::prefix, prefix_separator, keep_prefix, Environment::source, figment::providers::Env::prefixed, Env::raw
  python  env_prefix, env_prefix_target, EnvSettingsSource, dynaconf envvar_prefix
  note    the prefix is taken whole and compared byte for byte, as figment's `prefixed("APP_")` and pydantic's `env_prefix` take it; pydantic compares without case by default (observed: `app_port` read under `APP_`), which a POSIX environment does not. `read_env` reads the variables at once, where viper's `AutomaticEnv` looks one up at each `Get`; a variable whose name does not begin with the prefix is left out even where it is not UTF-8

capability config/env-nesting  a variable's name split into the keys of a nested setting
  heroes  config.EnvOptions.separator
  go      SetEnvKeyReplacer, EnvKeyReplacer, StringReplacer, KeyDelimiter
  rust    config::Environment::separator, figment::providers::Env::split
  python  env_nested_delimiter, env_nested_max_split
  note    `__` by default, pydantic's `env_nested_delimiter` as its documentation writes it and config-rs's `separator`; a name giving an empty key once split, as macOS's `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING` does, is left out rather than failing every program

capability config/env-case  a variable's name read in lower case
  heroes  config.EnvOptions.lower_keys
  go      viper's keys, which it compares without case
  rust    config::Environment::convert_case, with_convert_case, Case, figment::providers::Env::lowercase, value::Uncased, UncasedStr
  python  case_sensitive
  note    the keys of a file keep their case, as figment and config-rs keep them; viper lowers every key. Only a variable's keys are lowered, its ASCII letters

