  python  dynaconf Settings.as_int, pydantic `int` fields
  note    from a number with no fraction, or a text of decimal digits with an optional sign, white space at its ends left out and zeros before it read, as pydantic reads `" 8080 "` and `"007"` (observed); `"1_000"`, `"0x1F"` and `"1.0"` refused, which pydantic reads as 1000, refuses and reads as 1. viper's `GetInt` truncates 1.5 to 1 and reads `"010"` as 8 (observed); here 1.5 is refused and `"010"` is 10

