dropped
  go      viper.Viper, Option, Decoder, Encoder, Codec registries' interfaces beyond config/formats: the plumbing of one value a program holds; a `Settings` is a value
  go      SetFs: an `afero` file system for tests; a test writes files under `build/`
  go      WithLogger, Debug's writer: what is logged is the program's; `format_sources` gives the text
  go      SetConfigPermissions: the mode of a written file is `fs`'s
  rust    config::builder::DefaultState, BuilderState, Source, Map, Value::new, ValueKind: plumbing of a builder and of its value type, which `json.Value` is here
  rust    figment::Provider, providers::Format, value::Dict, value::Map, value::Tag, value::Empty, value::Num beyond config/int, util::nest, util::diff_paths, util::vec_tuple_map, Profile's string methods: a provider is a `Layer`, its value a `json.Value`
  rust    dotenvy::Result, dotenvy::Iter's iterator methods: a map is answered whole
  python  PydanticBaseSettingsSource, SettingsConfigDict's keys that configure a pydantic model and not its settings (title, frozen, str_* , validate_*, json_schema_*, ser_*, alias_generator and the rest): a record of the program is its own
  python  dotenv.main's imports (os, io, logging, pathlib, tempfile, OrderedDict, typing names), with_warn_for_invalid_lines, rewrite's context manager: module plumbing; a line refused fails, never warns
